The application constructs its transition multiplicities from admitted formation
occurrences and previously committed contact relations. The probability of an
outcome is the cardinality of its opportunity set divided by the complete positive
inventory. No flip probability is a primitive of the D.E.C. compiler or engine.

*Scope.* This is a finite computational specialization. Main admits continuations
and permits weights on that support; AFC specifies a stochastic representation
after a finite state and kernel are supplied. Neither source uniquely fixes this
application's counting convention or establishes a physical proton collision law.
The frozen 256-state chiral application remains a separate declared baseline.

= Source and preparation <retained-setup>

*Setup.* Main/Manual is bound to base revision `8c3149b9d3d9`, with the detached
R04 admission repair. AFC is bound to `5a25e8bd5bbc`. The detailed full hashes and
source-to-code map accompany the delivery. Main owns the definitions and scoped
mathematics; this downstream application owns its finite realization and evidence.

