Each of two distinct lineages retains two certified Monon formation occurrences
with opposite handed presentations. Their IDs instantiate one ordered block of
two and a two-member ancestral shell. Each target return carries the actual
`1:2` motif witness with enclosure 6, a simple six-edge H1 cycle and turnaround
at its third edge. The application also checks that motif chirality equals the
trace's initial branch role. A has three initial target returns and B has two.
Each field contains its one recurring target lineage; formation components are
retained evidence, not additional population members.

Membership and placement are fixed in this first domain. The population is a
count of two distinct members. No cell measure is declared, so no population
density is reported. Q4 vertices, native cuts, fibre roles, completed returns,
beats and octal coordinates remain distinct types. No frequency-doubling meaning
is assigned to an octave.

#pagebreak()
= Continuation inventory <retained-inventory>

*Construction.* For every ordered triple of distinct axes $(a,b,c)$ of Q4,
construct the word

```text
0, 2^a, 2^a xor 2^b, 2^a xor 2^b xor 2^c,
2^b xor 2^c, 2^c, 0.
```

The 24 words form the declared C6 family. Exclude words whose first axis is the
retained incoming slot, and words using any closed axis. The gate mask stays
fixed during an attempt. The resulting geometry count $G$ belongs to
$\{0,4,6,18\}$. The mandatory hinge is executed at turnaround; optional dwell is
structurally absent in this domain. H1 and fibre events have no combined kernel.

Every eligible word receives one opportunity from each of the two oppositely
oriented formation components. Additional opportunities come from each eligible
retained relation separately. A relation retains the actual unmatched completed
returns under a declared ordinal pairing, and a clipped list of contact-support
and directed reflection occurrences. Their Cartesian product is its token set.
Its sign routes tokens to the matching handed recipe. Unit counting, ordinal
pairing and sign routing are explicit application choices.

Let $r_0,r_1$ be the two retained signed contribution values, with separate
presence flags. Count their positive and negative tokens individually. With
$n_-$ and $n_+$ the resulting per-word counts,

$ Z = G (n_- + n_+), quad P(h,w) = n_h / Z quad (Z > 0). $

Signed contributions never become negative probability weights. A retained zero
has a presence record but contributes no tokens; absence has no such record.
Opposite nonzero contributions remain separately retained even when their sum
vanishes. They can have different future expiry and therefore cannot be replaced
by their signed sum in the predictive state.

*Atomic representation.* Retain the hand with probability
$P(h)=n_h/(n_-+n_+)$. Given that hand, condition the inventory on the executed
H1 prefix and count surviving words for each next edge. The edge conditional
probabilities telescope to $1/G$; multiplying by $P(h)$ gives the handed-word
probability above. A uniform token rank within that hand gives elementary
probability $1/Z$. The edge chain without a hand is only the geometric marginal:
initially $1/18$ per word, versus $1/36$ per handed word. Hinge entry is separate.
The single macro ticket selects this full joint inventory exactly; no independent
atomic resampling or probability-one closure outside the family is asserted.

*Exact selection.* The horizon is six attempts; each retained magnitude is at
most 42. Thus $n_-+n_+ <= 86$ and $Z <= 1548$. Use
$D = 36 thin "lcm"(1,2,dots,86)$ and an addressed integer $u$ in $[0,D)$.
Every positive total divides $D$. Select the first cumulative inventory count
$C$ satisfying $u Z < D C$. Matched interventions keep the same $u$ even if
their totals differ. No rounded percentage or modulo-biased ticket conversion
enters selection.

If $G=0$, preserve pending status and emit no new return certificate. Structural
absence remains distinct from a generalized admitted family with zero positive
weight. This application's surviving words always have formation opportunities.

#pagebreak()
= Recursive commitment and sufficient state <retained-update>

*Update.* Complete the selected C6 returns and append their full certificates
and motif witnesses. Preserve every previous prefix and lineage identity.
A contact is constructed only when both members complete during the attempt.
Its short support has two H1 traversals and one interior hinge role. Directional
reflection lists count actual completed-return hinge occurrences since the
previous contact. Their lengths are not guessed reflection constants.

The previous contact is eligible for a repeated-contact relation only within
the declared two-attempt window. Using the newly completed prefixes, let
$delta = N_A - N_B$. With old reflection counts $f_A,f_B$ and new since-contact
counts $s_A,s_B$, the new incoming contributions are

$ r_A = -chi_B min(6, 3+f_B+s_B) delta, $
$ r_B =  chi_A min(6, 3+f_A+s_A) delta. $

The coefficient 3 is this admitted contact support's accessor. The clipped
duration and unmatched-return tokens realize the product with unit capacity.
This is a newest-contact comparator with a two-contact RCD, explicitly distinct
from a convention summing every historical comparator. Both directions retain
their own provenance. After contact, reset the since-contact counts; advance
the two-slot retention queue without deleting the full archive.

*Causal order.* Attempt $t$ selects at native cut $60+18t$. Target closures
complete at $67+18t$, contact support at $70+18t$, and retention at $71+18t$.
The next selection is at $78+18t$. New retained information first affects a
later response. These integer indices are not seconds or a universal clock.

*Projection.* The scalar key contains the attempt index; both incoming slots,
handedness values, completed-return counts and since-contact counts; latest
contact age and directed reflection counts; and two separate signed retained
values with presence flags for each member. Gates and addressed tickets are
external inputs. Full witness identities and histories remain available outside
this predictive key.

For extraction $K$, complete update $F$ and scalar update $T$, sufficiency requires
both equal requested outputs for equal keys and
$ K(F(H,e)) = T(K(H),e). $
Every consumed operand and next coordinate is an explicit function of the key
and external input on keys extracted from valid reachable witness histories.
This proves closure of the projection for those scalar outputs. Scalar range
guards alone do not authenticate a history. Exact enumerations and witness extraction
checks test the implementation, including expiry and later response to new
retention. This is not a claim that all 20-coordinate combinations were
exhaustively enumerated or that the projection is universally minimal.

*Falsification controls.* Remove and restore retained relations with unchanged
world, closure memory and future tickets. Preserve cancelling nonzero terms,
present zero and absence. Close the return interfaces to test nonoperativity;
this domain has no separate coupling-only gate. A passing one-step comparison
does not replace the later expiry and newly committed response checks.

#pagebreak()
= Execution and observation boundary <retained-execution>

The host constructs the complete opportunity witnesses. The D.E.C. scalar
program computes counts, selection, expiry and next state from retained operands
and external masks/tickets. Each invocation consumes the previously computed
state. It receives no host-selected future chirality or precomputed future
relation. The compiler remains unchanged.

Reference execution and typed IR use the same source as LLVM AOT and ORC LLJIT.
Backend evidence records actual routes and optimization levels. Full Manual
formation/contact admission remains at the host boundary; scalar agreement alone
does not admit a complete witness. Read the delivered executable checks for
actual coverage, failures and unsupported routes. The older CUDA and multicore
frozen-law evidence does not certify this new update. This construction makes
no cost-inclusive speedup, M6 self-hosting or AArch64 claim.

*Preparation and observation.* The computational preparation is the bound pair
of motif histories, contact seed, fixed membership and gate/ticket input stream.
Its direct outputs are selected atomic paths, completed returns, contact records,
retained contributions and exact conditional probabilities. An experimental
preparation, moving detector boundary and packet-to-observation map have not
been supplied. Return counts cannot be relabelled as measured oscillator turns.

The existing Manual SI interface remains separately bound in
`simulations/manual_si_fixture.py`, consuming Manual
`eq:manual-m3-accumulated-si`. It requires compared and reference observed phase
advances, a common coordinate/epoch/window and a declared reference realization.
This continuation construction supplies none of that physical correspondence.
It therefore reports no collision energy, cross-section, microwave frequency,
seconds per return, or physical accuracy percentage.

